# M7.1 (2026-06-21): on-chip XOR TRAINING with the backward input-grad Wᵀ·δ ALSO
# on the 4x4 INT8 array (transpose-load), forward W·x on the array too; loss/δ/
# outer-product/SGD in NEORV32 SW. Same DFX static structure as M6.3 (rm_tpuvpu,
# VPU bypassed); only the IMEM image differs. Loss curve via PS mailbox 0x41200000
# (scripts/m7-watch-loss.py). Built from vivado/dfx build impl_5.
# Firmware has a ~10s post-config SETTLE delay before training (M7_SETTLE_ITERS):
# without it training diverges from ep0 on real silicon (deterministic garbage) even
# though isolated maccs read correct — the cure is wall-clock time, not warm-up count.
# A single-boot settle-time sweep measured the minimum at ~1-2s (≤5s confirmed); 10s is
# a safe margin (was 45s). This hash is the ~10s SETTLE build (hw-verified: full loss
# curve bit-exact to oracle, XOR 4/4, SSE=0).
# (Supersedes the M7.0b builds 2658438e / 76f2a46a, which did Wᵀ·δ in SW Q8.8.)
ec6716c8006a97e8775ced297e77e2a563df5316fc4c021235ff6d3e80d7ce12  full-static+RM_TPUVPU-M7TRAIN
eb776cc21953f4d1c43a7f517264a1927489dd27c9da56238231220a62ac8853  partial-RM_TPUVPU-M7TRAIN
# M7.3 (2026-06-27): DFX train<->infer split + measured-boot gate, path (a) (verified
# single-step). rm_train = HW train_unit trio + 4x4 INT8 array on the tpu_rp interface
# (cfg8/impl_8). The M5 gate now authorizes BOTH the trainer (this hash) AND the
# inference RM (partial-RM_TPUVPU above) so a loadbp swap between them is measured at
# each step (M6.4 measure-then-yield). Single-step compute on rm_train is hw-verified
